  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Secretary-General&apos;s Good Offices</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Good Offices programme reinforces the capacity of the Secretary-General&apos;s preventive diplomacy and quiet political engagements for strengthening democratic resilience in member countries. The Good Offices Section (GOS) follows a comprehensive peacebuilding strategy that balances short-term crisis response with long-term structural conflict prevention. In the short term, it uses intensive preventive diplomacy to address immediate or ongoing disputes before they escalate into violence. In the long term, it focuses on addressing the underlying causes of conflict through sustained engagement. The Good Offices programme is also delivered in two interconnected components: track 1 which is a high-level political track led by the Secretary-General, the Commonwealth Ministerial Action Group (CMAG), the Commonwealth-Chair-in Office and Commonwealth Special Envoys and; and a technical track which provides targeted and tailored support to member states. Track 2 involves deploying capacity building for strengthening national political dialogues and early warning and peacebuilding architectures, and facilitating peace agreements, negotiations and pledges. Good Offices work contributes to Secretariat&apos;s programme for strengthening inclusive governance and democratic resilience by providing advice and strategies informed by political intelligence on countries with democratic stressors affecting youth and other marginalised groups.</narrative>
  </description>
